WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.160
It’s one of those sequels that’s been
rumored for years: Goonies 2.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:09.179
The latest surge of Goonies hype happened
in 2014, when director Richard Donner confirmed

00:00:09.179 --> 00:00:14.589
that the long-awaited sequel was indeed going
ahead, but so far… nothing.

00:00:14.589 --> 00:00:18.930
Unfortunately for Goonies everywhere, a sequel
becomes increasingly unlikely with every passing

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:19.930
year.

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:22.650
Here's why we never got to see The Goonies
2.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.060
The scripts have sucked

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:29.440
In 2009, Empire magazine conducted an interview
with all of the original Goonies, as well

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:34.329
as director Richard Donner and producer Steven
Spielberg, and naturally, the interview soon

00:00:34.329 --> 00:00:35.989
turned to talk of a sequel.

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:40.329
Donner was quick to blame the lack of a decent
screenplay for the film's constant stalling,

00:00:40.329 --> 00:00:44.969
telling Empire that he and Spielberg had spent
a lot of energy hunting for a good script,

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:48.809
and that the duo "had many meetings with writers,
but nothing stuck."

00:00:48.809 --> 00:00:53.640
Cast member and weird modern vampire Corey
Feldman was more positive about the prospect

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.970
of a second Goonies outing, though Donner
didn't share his enthusiasm, stating there

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:01.219
was "no hope" of it going ahead at that stage.

00:01:01.219 --> 00:01:06.550
Even Feldman, who doesn’t have much going
on right now except for...whatever this is...knows

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:09.420
that Goonies 2 is a dangerous game to play,
saying,

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.040
"It could have a very bad backlash!

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:16.450
At the end of the day, and I have said this
before, the only way a Goonies sequel happens,

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:19.590
and is forgivable to the fanbase, is if it
is done right."

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:24.130
Feldman and co-star Sean Astin even wrote
a sequel themselves and presented it to Richard

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:27.340
Donner, but were told that their ideas were
too expensive.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:31.720
Considering how much cash goes into blockbusters
today, and the fact that animated prosthetics

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:35.510
and a giant pirate ship weren’t too cost
prohibitive for the original, it’s hard

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:39.480
to imagine what Feldman and Astin turned in
that was deemed too extravagant.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:42.040
But either way, Astin is game.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.800
“Yes or no: Goonies sequel.”

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:44.800
“Someday.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:45.560
I hope.”

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:46.220
“You in?”

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:47.140
“If they want me.”

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.000
“Alright!”

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:48.500
“Yes!

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:49.000
Yes!

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:49.500
Yes!”

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.060
And everyone knows, an angry Al Roker will
not be denied.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.070
“Spielberg!

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:55.440
Get on it!

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:57.799
Make The Goonies 2!”

00:01:57.799 --> 00:02:01.530
Producer Frank Marshall has gone on record
as saying that he won't make a sequel just

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:05.770
for the sake of doing it, insisting that the
story has to be right before the film can

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.410
go ahead to avoid disappointing fans.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:13.140
Ironically, fans ended up being disappointed
by another one of his comments…

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:15.070
A reboot instead?

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:19.130
Picture this: a bunch of middle-aged Goonies
have lost touch with what it means to be a

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:23.700
member of the team, leaving their children
to revive their never-say-die attitude and

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.280
take them on a new adventure.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.070
It writes itself, right?

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:29.330
Frank Marshall doesn't quite see it that way.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:33.670
The producer revealed that any new Goonies
project would not actually be a sequel, but

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:37.010
a film made "in the Amblin spirit of Goonies."

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:41.800
So, unfortunately for those hoping for a continuation
of the story, the idea of a complete reboot

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:45.520
has been supported by the writer of the original
movie, Chris Columbus.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:49.330
Despite previously stating that the only way
the film could be done was with the original

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:53.830
kids as parents, Columbus has since changed
his tune, confirming that he’s currently

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:58.980
on a full nostalgia-attack, and actively involved
in reboots of both The Goonies and Gremlins.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:04.350
“Look, there are a lot of writers who are
interested in writing Goonies, but the problem

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:09.260
is that we’re very protective because it’s,
it’s a, such a well-loved movie.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.440
The same goes for Gremlins.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.260
Gremlins is a little easier…”

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:15.400
Because that worked out so well for Ghostbusters.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.490
Richard Donner is getting older

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:22.180
As someone who’s keen to see this long-awaited
sequel eventually happen, Feldman has raised

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:25.260
fears that the project is very much time sensitive,
saying,

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.940
"Richard Donner is 87 years old.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:30.930
And it's like, no one really wants to make
it without him.

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:32.770
He's the driving force behind it.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:34.210
He says it's still alive.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:38.650
But as we all know, when you get to that age,
things slow down quite a bit.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:42.040
There is a big possibility that he might not
want to keep driving it."

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:45.790
Feldman went on to explain that Goonies 2
just wouldn't happen without Donner in the

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:50.130
director's chair, adding that every day that
passes without the wheels in motion takes

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:52.810
us a day closer to it never happening.

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.120
Chunk out

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:57.851
Even if Goonies 2 is a sequel, they would
have been forced to do it without one of the

00:03:57.851 --> 00:03:59.771
most loved of all the Goonies.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:08.260
[Retching sounds]

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:13.230
Jeff Cohen, the former child actor who played
Chunk, nixed the idea of returning, claiming

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:17.930
that his new career as an entertainment attorney
and author is too good to give up, even if

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:20.040
he does remember his acting days fondly.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:23.630
“Anybody who says they intentionally give
up acting is lying.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.630
They’re absolutely lying.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:29.940
Uh, you know, I loved being a kid actor, it
was great, but you know for me I look different,

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:34.340
I was evolving from Chunk to hunk, that I
am today.”

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:38.470
Cohen has become one of the go-to attorneys
in Hollywood, has written a book called The

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:43.250
Dealmaker's Ten Commandments, and the ex-Goonie
also occasionally writes about legal and political

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:44.660
matters for CNBC.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:49.160
So, he probably doesn’t have enough time
to do the ol’ Truffle Shuffle anymore.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:53.540
“Ohhhaaaaoohhh.”

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:56.100
Goonies go off-Broadway

00:04:56.100 --> 00:05:00.130
Evidently fed up with waiting for a sequel
to be greenlit, Donner went ahead and made

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:03.060
alternate arrangements to bring the Goonies
back to life.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:07.850
In 2015, the director announced that he was
creating an off-Broadway, immersive production

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:08.960
of The Goonies.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.900
He outlined his vision to Yahoo!

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:11.980
Movies, explaining,

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:16.070
"There's no seats, the venue is you go into
a warehouse and there's something happening

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:20.210
in that warehouse and that's the play you've
come to see, only you become part of it and

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.660
you travel through with actors."

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:26.220
The Goonies play has yet to materialize, with
no details to speak of.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:30.150
Donner was adamant that the show would soon
be a reality, however, and while this would

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:35.330
surely be an unforgettable experience for
any Goonies fan, Donner focusing on this project

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:38.770
means Goonies 2 is as far off now as it's
ever been.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:42.530
The closest we’ll ever get is a notoriously
weird Nintendo game.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:46.700
But never say die, right?

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:47.730
“Don’t say that!

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:48.760
Never say that!

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:50.130
Goonies never say die!”

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:51.460
Thanks for watching!

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:54.270
